# Fixed 2026-11-13, defect 2494, lane b35-signals (panel 247's door G), its
# two-module shape: one module watches SIGUSR1, another takes the count.
# Symptom: a handler of C's in a header the program ships keeps its flag
# `static`, so two modules that include the header hold two flags, and the
# module asking read the one no handler set: SIGINT ignored 2 runs of 2 at
# exit 0 (panel 247's spec-warden, `swp6`).
# Cause: the runtime's door is one counter per process, in the runtime's one
# translation unit, so the module that takes reads what the module that
# watched made count. The program sends itself SIGUSR1 three times.
use counter

extern "unistd.h"
    function getpid() -> i32

extern "signal.h"
    constant SIGUSR1: i32
    function kill(pid: i32, sig: i32) -> i32

extern "hero_os.h"
    function hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64

function main()
    print("watching SIGUSR1 here: ", hero_signal_watch(sig: SIGUSR1))
    sent @= 0

    while sent < 3
        _ = kill(pid: getpid(), sig: SIGUSR1)
        sent @ sent + 1

    print("sent ", sent, ", taken in the other module ", counter.taken())
